}}|subdivision_type1=[[Communities of Balisca|Community]]|subdivision_name1={{flag|Bayara}}|area_km2=64,444.39|population_census=1,837,599|population_census_year=2025|regional_languages=|common_languages={{W|Aragonese language|Aragonese}}, [[Baliscano]], {{W|Catalan language|Catalan}}, {{W|Sabir language|Sabir}}|cctld=.aba|mapsize=280px|demonym=Abellesian <br> Abellés|ethnic_groups_year=2025|ethnic_groups=74.2% [[Baliscans]]<br/> 25.8% [[Demographics of Balisca|others]]}}'''Abellesia''' ({{Literal translation|place of bees}}; {{Langx|kp|Eíra-Ka'a|4=honey forest}}) is a geographically diverse and heavily forested [[regions of Balisca|autonomous region]] in northern [[Bayara]] within the [[Western Plains (Balisca)|Western Plains]] {{W|ecoregion}}. It is frequently praised for its dramatic scenery that has remained relatively pristine throughout history. The [[Rural society in Balisca|regional culture]], mountainous interior and coastal marshes/grasslands, and other recreational opportunities have made Abellesia a popular destination for visitors from across the world. 

